@*

Modal<TEntity> — Pure Blazor, State-Driven Modal Component

Purpose
-------
This component implements a Bootstrap-styled modal dialog that is **entirely
controlled in C#**, without Bootstrap JavaScript or JS interop.

It serves as a reusable, generic modal shell capable of hosting CRUD forms,
including multi-stage workflows involving dependent entities.

The modal is not a passive visual wrapper; it owns its visibility, focus,
keyboard handling, and backdrop interaction semantics.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Core Design Principles
----------------------
• Fully C#-controlled (no JSRuntime, no Bootstrap JS)
• Explicit state machine (Visible / Shown)
• Deterministic focus ownership
• Keyboard-accessible (Esc handling)
• Backdrop behavior modeled explicitly via enum
• Parent-controlled intent, modal-controlled mechanics

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Visibility & State Model
------------------------
The modal maintains two internal visibility flags:

• IsVisible
  - Controls whether the modal/backdrop are rendered and displayed.
  - Governs tabindex participation and DOM presence.

• IsShown
  - Controls Bootstrap "show" CSS class.
  - Enables entry/exit animations.

Show() and Hide() manipulate these flags in a specific order to preserve
animation timing while keeping the component deterministic.

The modal **owns its internal visibility**, while the parent is notified via
OnVisibilityChanged for app-level side effects (e.g., body scroll locking).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Focus & Accessibility Contract
-------------------------------
• The modal root is focusable **only when visible**
  (tabindex="0" when visible, "-1" when hidden).
• Focus is programmatically moved to the modal root on Show().
• ESC key handling is attached directly to the modal root.
• Hidden modals are completely removed from the tab order.

This mirrors Bootstrap’s runtime behavior while remaining fully declarative.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Backdrop Semantics
------------------
Backdrop behavior is modeled explicitly using ModalBackdrop:

• Enabled
  - Backdrop is rendered.
  - Clicking outside the dialog closes the modal.

• Static
  - Backdrop is rendered.
  - Clicking outside the dialog does nothing.

• Disabled
  - No backdrop is rendered.
  - All clicks fall through to the page.

Important Design Note:
Backdrop clicks are **not** handled on the backdrop element itself.
Instead, the modal root acts as the full-screen interaction surface:

• The modal root captures clicks.
• The dialog stops propagation.
• Close logic is conditionally executed based on Backdrop mode.

This avoids fragile pointer-events CSS hacks and ensures consistent behavior.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Keyboard & Mouse Interaction
----------------------------
• ESC key closes the modal via HandleKeyDown.
• Backdrop clicks are processed via HandleBackdropClicked.
• Dialog clicks stop propagation explicitly.

All interaction rules are enforced in C#, not CSS or JavaScript.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Content & Staging
-----------------
The modal supports multi-stage workflows via ModalStage:

• MainForm
• DependentForm

Content is injected using RenderFragment parameters, allowing the parent
component to control form composition without the modal knowing domain details.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Public API (Conceptual)
-----------------------
Parameters:
• Item                      — Entity instance being edited/viewed
• Operation                 — CRUD operation indicator
• Title                     — Modal title text
• BtnSubmitText             — Submit button label
• Size                      — ModalSize enum
• Backdrop                  — ModalBackdrop enum
• Stage                     — ModalStage enum
• MainFormContent           — Primary form fragment
• DependentFormContent      — Dependent form fragment
• OnSubmit                  — Submit action callback
• OnClose                   — Close intent callback
• OnVisibilityChanged(bool) — Visibility notification hook

Methods:
• Show() — Displays modal, sets focus, triggers animation
• Hide() — Hides modal, releases focus, reverses animation

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Explicit Non-Goals
------------------
• No automatic body manipulation
• No implicit JS-based behavior
• No global state ownership
• No hard dependency on CRUD semantics

The modal is a **mechanical UI component**, not an application controller.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
End of Modal<TEntity> documentation
===============================================================================
*@

@typeparam TEntity
@using blazor_hcom.Models

@namespace blazor_hcom.Components.Layout

@* The Backdrop shows only if the Modal is visible and its state is not disabled .*@
@if (IsVisible && Backdrop != ModalBackdrop.Disabled)
{
	<div class="@BackdropClass"></div>
}

@*
  - Interaction: Modal layer now handles backdrop clicks because it 
    visually obscures the actual backdrop div.
  - Event Flow: Used stopPropagation on .modal-dialog to isolate internal 
    clicks from the dismissal logic.
*@
<div class="modal @(Fading ? "fade" : "") @(IsShown ? "show" : "")"
	 tabindex="@(IsVisible ? "0" : "-1")"
	 id="theModal"
	 @ref="_modalRoot"
	 @onkeydown="HandleKeyDown"
	 @onclick="HandleBackdropClicked"
	 style="@(IsVisible ? "display: block;" : "display: none;")">
	<div class="modal-dialog @ModalSizeClass" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
		<div class="modal-content">
			<div class="modal-header">
				<h3 class="modal-title" id="theModalTitle">@Title</h3>
				<button class="btn btn-close" @onclick="OnClose"></button>
			</div>
			<div class="modal-body">
				@if (Stage == ModalStage.MainForm) {
					@MainFormContent
				}
				else if (Stage == ModalStage.DependentForm) {
					@DependentFormContent
				}
			</div>
			<div class="modal-footer">
				@if(Operation != "read"){
					<button class="btn btn-secondary rounded-pill" type="button"
						@onclick="OnClose" id="theModalButtonCancel ">Cancel</button>
				}
				<button class="btn btn-primary rounded-pill" type="button"
							   id="theModalButtonSubmit" @onclick="OnSubmit">@BtnSubmitText</button>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
